Project Mu: give Mu its own profile folder on Windows

kProductPathName names the folder under %LOCALAPPDATA% that holds the
browser's User Data, and the HKCU\Software key it writes. Upstream it is
"Chromium", so Mu shared its profile with any other Chromium on the machine,
and another Chromium's history or cookies could end up in Mu (and the other
way round). Mu now uses %LOCALAPPDATA%\Project Mu\User Data.

Windows only; the file is not built on other platforms.

diff --git a/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h b/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
index a6d969d..7c24e5b 100644
--- a/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
+++ b/chrome/install_static/chromium_install_modes.h
@@ -21,7 +21,9 @@ inline constexpr wchar_t kCompanyPathName[] = L"";
 
 // The brand-specific product name to be included as a component of the install
 // and user data directory paths.
-inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Chromium";
+// Project Mu: keep Mu's profile (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Project Mu\User Data) and
+// registry key (HKCU\Software\Project Mu) apart from any other Chromium.
+inline constexpr wchar_t kProductPathName[] = L"Project Mu";
 
 // The brand-specific safe browsing client name.
 inline constexpr char kSafeBrowsingName[] = "chromium";
